S2 - Mod Call Handling
When answering a mod-call, you are required to always be incredibly professional to any extent. Our goal is to facilitate a big community, and for that, we require a professional staff team. When you answer the mod call, you should make it a priority to attempt a greeting, via Discord voice channels or text chat (when appropriate.) If you believe the user is not in your age group, you may use :pm <user> <text>. Remember that you are required to use SPaG whilst private messaging a user, unless you are off-duty.
Once you have entered a staff scene with the caller, ask them for the reason for the call. If they are reporting another player, you are required to receive a legible clip of the offense taking place, otherwise you cannot moderate it. If the evidence is valid, you may moderate it at your discretion.
You are always required to log punishments via Melonly after moderating a player.
If you are vision seat certified, then you are allowed to moderate members via Melonly Vision, which has logging built into it.
Moderating through the Staff Panel is also simple. Simply look up a player, select the punishment, fill out the reason, and Melonly will take care of it for you. If you file a Ban BOLO, please attach the evidence / clip to the reason or provided field.
If you kick a member, you must always:
A. Notify the member that they are being kicked for <reason>
B. Make it known that they may not rejoin for 25 minutes or they will be kicked again automatically, resetting their timer





